@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# Local integration and validation record
+
+This development build starts from upstream PdfCraft commit
+`5644d56c64af1529b0f9012874886fcad855c257`. It combines independently reusable
+Rust OpenScan integration, document Undo/Redo toolbar controls, focused search and
+platform fixes, and selected existing upstream proposals.
+
+## Existing upstream contributions
+
+The following work retains its original upstream provenance. Reusing it here does
+not imply that the original project has merged it or approved this combined build.
+Do not open duplicate pull requests for these contributions.
+
+| Contribution | Upstream pull request | Reviewed revision |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Wheel scrolling over the inactive window under the pointer | [#6329](https://github.com/storytold/pdfcraft/pull/6329) | `b8329435d0b40acc964bef6419d58957e23b1782` |
+| Pin recent documents across clears, new opens and restarts | [#4885](https://github.com/storytold/pdfcraft/pull/4885) | `e38c642d68386197e2a43ac8875563713e929544` |
+| Editable registered-command keyboard shortcuts | [#4646](https://github.com/storytold/pdfcraft/pull/4646) | `64648b6f5a967350b2f956aa5b39aa3a6309657e` |
+
+The inactive-window regression was reproduced before importing the fix. The full
+interface suite, strict Clippy, formatting, layer/asset checks, WebAssembly checks,
+and Windows application/CLI builds passed afterward. These are automated checks;
+an actual inactive native window still needs an interactive check.
+
+Pinning was checked with the upstream behavior test and an additional regression
+that exercised a missing file after restart. The added regression failed before
+integration and both passed afterward. The imported fixture now creates its own
+directory exclusively and removes only its three known files, followed by the
+empty directory; it does not recursively remove a pre-existing temporary path.
+
+The shortcut control-channel regression failed before importing its implementation
+and passed afterward. Local adjustments make the imported tests check Windows,
+Linux and macOS modifier labels, keep system Copy in the read-only keys list, and
+omit empty shortcut parentheses from the Undo/Redo toolbar tooltips. Combined
+application gates and native platform checks must pass before this integration
+is presented as ready.
+
+## Rust scanner
+
+[OpenScan](https://github.com/kevin7du-cpu/openscan/tree/rust-portability/rust) uses
+Rust and PdfCraft's pinned egui/eframe and craft-ui/craft-dialogs dependencies.
+It provides standalone Scan and Manage presets interfaces and a versioned JSON
+process protocol. The same scanner binary can be reused by another application;
+`openscan-core` and `openscan-ui` also support direct Rust integration.
+
+Windows, Linux and macOS scanner tests, strict Clippy and release builds passed at
+`6b5947858ea71f4a946fa465b7122ae507779b20` in
+[the recorded CI run](https://github.com/kevin7du-cpu/openscan/actions/runs/42421535463).
+Linux exercised an installed SANE test backend with size and DPI checks. The Windows
+release binary passed an offline OCR/PDF round trip with independent PdfCraft text
+extraction and rendering. These checks do not establish real-device compatibility.
+See [scanner capabilities and limits](scanner.md).
+
+## Other local corrections
+
+Advanced Search handles Up/Down from its query field or a clicked result without
+changing the query or taking keys from another text field. Its regression was
+observed failing with the old implementation and passing with the correction.
+
+A bundled macOS application leaves its icon to AppKit, preserving Finder icon
+customization. Unbundled launches and other platforms retain the embedded icon.
+The viewport uses eframe's explicit empty-icon sentinel: leaving its icon unset
+would substitute the framework's logo. Both the bundle-path decision and the
+framework-boundary regression were observed failing before their respective
+corrections. Native macOS Finder/Dock verification remains pending.
+
+The interface's ArtCraft trademark mark is replaced by an existing generic
+document icon, and trademarked brand artwork is omitted in accordance with the
+repository's fork policy. The separately MIT/Apache-licensed PdfCraft app icon is
+retained. No proprietary scanner SDK, C# companion, .NET, OpenCV or Tesseract runtime
+is part of the Rust build.
+
+## Outstanding verification
+
+Physical acquisition through the Rust build, duplex/device-specific behavior,
+native desktop dialogs, real Linux/macOS scanners, and the remaining feature
+requests require further work. Signing was tested headlessly with a public sample
+and synthetic credentials; native signing-dialog interaction remains pending.
+This record must not be read as a claim that every requested feature is complete
+or that the combined build is an official release.
